In article <8APR199321240589@eql.caltech.edu>, rankin@eql.caltech.edu (Pat Rankin) writes:
 > In article <1993Apr8.144731.14495@nmr-z.mgh.harvard.edu>,\
 >  tcb@cipr-fellow.nmr writes...
 > > Is there a way to get the numeric keypad on a sun keyboard to work properly
 > > as movement keys?  I can get terminals to work fine, but the sun keys don't
 > > want to work...
 > 
 >      NetHack's number_pad mode uses digit characters for movement commands.
 > You need to figure out how to get your keyboard's keypad keys to transmit
 > simple digits instead of escape sequences.  I think people have posted one
 > or more ways to accomplish that at some time or other.
 > 
Put the following in your .Xdefaults file, start X and type
xterm -name hack &
You will get an xterm with remapped kepad keys. This works on suns and some
DEC machines.  If you want to free up the hjklbnyu keys you may use
the number_pad option and insert numbers instead of letters.

!#
!# nethack
!#
hack*vt100*geometry: 80x24
hack*vt100*scrollBar: off
hack*vt100.Translations: #override \
        <Key>Left: string("B")\n\
        <Key>Down: string("J")\n\
        <Key>Right: string("N")\n\
        <Key>Select: string("H")\n\
        <Key>Next: string("L")\n\
        <Key>Find: string("Y")\n\
        <Key>Insert: string("K")\n\
        <Key>apLineDel: string("U2")\n\
        <Key>KP_1: string("b")\n\
        <Key>KP_2: string("j")\n\
        <Key>KP_3: string("n")\n\
        <Key>KP_4: string("h")\n\
        <Key>KP_5: string(".")\n\
        <Key>KP_6: string("l")\n\
        <Key>KP_7: string("y")\n\
        <Key>KP_8: string("k")\n\
        <Key>KP_9: string("u")\n\
        <Key>R13: string("b")\n\
        <Key>R14: string("j")\n\
        <Key>R15: string("n")\n\
        <Key>R10: string("h")\n\
